# --- the way up is NOT here ------------------------------------------------
#
# `jib_vi_walk.loom` leans a drawn 42 degree plank against the flybridge,
# because the mesh's own ladder is unclimbable by construction: 0.75 m between
# rungs against a 0.35 m step height, an 0.08 m tread against a 0.35 m capsule
# radius, and 68 degrees against a 50 degree slope limit.
#
# It is **not** in this prefab, and the reason is small and worth stating: the
# plank is the one piece that is *drawn*, so it needs a `box` asset, and a
# prefab's asset key is renamed on merge when the consuming scene already
# declares one by that name — `box` becomes `box_2`, which resolves to no
# built-in and draws a unit cube with a warning. Every other node here is
# collision only and declares nothing.
#
# So the flybridge is reachable in `jib_vi_walk.loom` and not from this prefab.
# A scene that wants it up there authors its own plank as a child of the boat;
# `assets/test/jib_vi_walk.loom` has the transform. Nothing in
# `assets/games/deeper_demo.loom` goes up there — its helm is a mat on the aft
# deck — which is why this is a note rather than a blocker.
